<title>USA: USDA DONATES 4,000 TONNES SOYMEAL TO EL SALVADOR.</title>
<headline>USDA DONATES 4,000 TONNES SOYMEAL TO EL SALVADOR.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said on Thursday that it is donating 4,000 tonnes of soymeal to a private voluntary group in El Salvador.</p>
<p>The soymeal will be sold to local buyers to raise funds for a health education program aimed at reducing deaths from water-borne illnesses, USDA said.</p>
<p>The supply period for the donation is fiscal 1997, which ends September 30.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8341))</p>
